umask 022
: 'Clear the /tmp MOUNT POINT, before hd3 is mounted over it.  Anything'
: 'written to /tmp in single user -- before this script runs at all -- landed'
: 'in the root file system here, where the mount below then hides it for the'
: 'rest of the session.  Nothing else ever looks in this directory, so it is'
: 'swept now or never.  The real /tmp is cleared further down, AFTER the'
: 'mount that makes it real.'
rm -f /tmp/* /tmp/.??*
>/etc/mnttab
>/etc/utmp
/etc/swap&
/etc/mount /dev/hd0 / -u
: '-c: repair a file system that was not cleanly unmounted with check -s'
: 'here, then mount it read/write, instead of coming up read only.  Not'
: 'for the root -u above -- the kernel mounted it and marks it dirty on'
: 'disk while it is in use -- nor for the read only /v.'
/etc/mount /dev/hd1 /u -c
/etc/mount /dev/hd2 /v -r
/etc/mount /dev/hd3 /tmp -c
chmod 777 /tmp
: 'NOW clear /tmp: hd3 is what /tmp actually IS, so a sweep before the mount'
: 'reached only the empty directory underneath it and every real temporary'
: 'survived the boot.  The second pattern matters as much as the timing --'
: 'a bare * never matched a dot file, and the GUI text stores are all dot'
: 'files (selection bodies /tmp/.hrsel<pid>, the clipboard /tmp/.hrclip and'
: 'any /tmp/.hrclipn<pid> a Copy died holding), so they accumulated for ever.'
: '.??* needs three characters, which is how . and .. are kept out of it.'
rm -f /tmp/* /tmp/.??*
/etc/update&
/etc/cron&
date >/dev/console
: "hr windowing system: start the GUI desktop only when explicitly enabled"
: "-- create the flag with:  touch /etc/hrgui .  hrconsole loads /drv/hr,"
: "which seizes the keyboard IRQ and the bitmap framebuffer, so it REPLACES"
: "the text console.  Off by default so serial-console and video-less"
: "emulator boots are unaffected.  See SMGR.md for the startup sequence."
if [ -f /etc/hrgui ]; then /usr/hr/bin/hrconsole & fi
: "ZView, see GUI.md: the single-server window system + clock/terminal"
: "windows.  Enable with:  touch /etc/wgui .  zview loads /drv/hr itself,"
: "so it also replaces the text console; off by default.  Root is already"
: "read-write here, mounted -u above, which the server pipe IPC needs."
if [ -f /etc/wgui ]; then /usr/hr/bin/zview & fi
